      "content": "While it's true that you have experienced migraines before, this new combination of symptoms warrants a visit to the emergency room. Even if you think it's just a \"bad\" aura, you're taking a risk by not seeking medical attention. Migraines can be a sign of an underlying condition, and ignoring your concerns may lead to more serious complications. Additionally, medical professionals can assess your symptoms and run tests to rule out other potential causes, such as a Transient Ischemic Attack (TIA) or a stroke.",
